{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261113-flow1","sourceHashNormalization":"utf8-lf-v1","scope":"Context-preserving topic lessons, explicit lesson-preset checks, editable experiment drafts, choice-specific remediation, optional first-use matrix bridges, and consistent Lie stage navigation.","counts":{"topicFamilies":14,"topicModules":40,"topicLessons":133,"topicExercises":133,"nonFirstLessonFlows":93,"foundationBridgeLessons":3,"optionalConceptBridges":4,"questionsWithChoiceFeedback":10,"independentRemediationQuestions":20},"verification":["Production UI event handlers test all 93 non-first lessons across 14 families: same-lesson return, explicit preset initialization, intermediate derivation state and editable drafts without automatic computation.","The 79 explicit course-return links retain lesson context. The 14 material browsing links keep their distinct material-route meaning.","Choice-specific repair and changed-condition questions do not increment the original question progress; changing a checked original answer revokes its checked state.","Four optional matrix bridges use local exact rational examples, noncommuting function actions and 104 unimodular coordinate transformations.","Seven Lie stage filters agree across the sidebar, chapter picker and next action; other lessons remain in a labelled native disclosure and cross-stage navigation offers a bounded return."],"limitations":["These are interface and mathematical-reference checks, not student learning-outcome measurements or a complete semantic audit of all lessons.","The optional geometric examples use two-dimensional teaching models; the generic rational rotation is not claimed to be a periodic-crystal operation.","Explicit lesson-preset actions intentionally initialize the documented experiment. Ordinary tab changes preserve custom input instead.","The Kanamori common-energy shift assumes fixed particle number, fixed J and crystal-field terms, and U-prime linked to U minus 2J; it is not a statement abou